  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: A ridge of high pressure will move\neastward across the Silver State this afternoon through Tuesday. A\nwarming trend is expected today and Tuesday. High temperatures\nthroughout Northern and Central Nevada this afternoon will be\naround five degrees warmer than yesterday afternoon. Maximum\ntemperatures across Northern and Central Nevada Tuesday afternoon\nwill be about five degrees warmer than this afternoon. \n\nAn upper-level area of low pressure will move eastward over\nCentral Nevada Tuesday night, resulting in a chance of light\nprecipitation. Snow levels will start at around 7,000 feet Tuesday\nevening, before dropping to about 6,000 feet Tuesday night. The\nmajority of this precipitation will be confined to White Pine\nCounty. Precipitation should end by 4 AM PST Wednesday morning. \n\nA ridge of high pressure will build northward across the Silver\nState Thursday through Sunday. As a result, dry weather is\nexpected in Northern and Central Nevada. A warming trend is\nanticipated Thursday through Sunday. By Sunday afternoon, high\ntemperatures across Northern and Central Nevada will be around\nfive degrees above normal for this time of year.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding a warming trend today and Tuesday. Moderate forecast\nconfidence in light precipitation in Central Nevada Tuesday night.\nModerate forecast confidence regarding dry weather Wednesday\nthrough at least Sunday. Moderate forecast confidence in gradual\nwarming Thursday through Sunday. No deviations or adjustments to\nthe NBM model output.",
